ery dimension  ending up with 1000 maximum values that  form your embedding of the input cloud  so by using the symmetric function we  got rid of the permutation sensitivity  while also not really carrying how many  points we actually put in here because  we always end up with 1000 values and  this resulting embedding you can then  process to for example classify whether  the input model is a plane or a chair  aside from permutation invariants you  have a bunch of other issues though not  properly defined convolution operator  varying densities you'd get from a laser  scanner etc and lots of more fun with  geometry and that's just the issues you  have for point clouds triangle measures  are even worse if you ask me so thank  you for staying with me until the end if  you have any cool suggestions for  community questions just send them and  we will credit you hope to see you again

